range the array to put each number in its correct index.  \\n   - **Second Pass**: Find the first index where `nums[i] != i + 1`.  \\n3. **Return**: If all positions match, return `n + 1`.  \\n\\n### Code Implementation:  \\n```python  \\ndef firstMissingPositive(nums):  \\n    n = len(nums)  \\n    for i in range(n):  \\n        while 1 <= nums[i] <= n and nums[nums[i] - 1] != nums[i]:  \\n            # Swap the elements  \\n            nums[nums[i] - 1], nums[i] = nums[i], nums[nums[i] - 1]  \\n    for i in range(n):  \\n        if nums[i] != i + 1:  \\n            return i + 1  \\n    return n + 1  \\n```  \\n\\n### Explanation of the Code:  \\n- Iterate through the list with a while loop to swap elements into their correct positions.  \\n- Finally, check the positions to find the first missing integer.  \\n### Time Complexity:  \\nO(n)  \\n### Space Complexity:  \\nO(1)  \\n\\nThis approach efficiently finds the solution while rearranging the elements in place!", "notification_type": "Leetcode"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Successfully sent notification to the device with echonoti. Time of notification: 2025-06-26T14:43:22.711Z.', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_Ivpf779cvNjt4M2cMm4biHzk'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'stream': False, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'set_alarm_at_specific_time', 'description': 'Sets an alarm to trigger at an absolute date/time in the future.\n\nParameters:\n    time (str): Exact trigger time in strict format:\n        "YYYY:MM:DD:HH:MM:SS" where:\n        - YYYY: 4-digit year (e.g., 2024)\n        - MM: Month (01-12, zero-padded)\n        - DD: Day (01-31, zero-padded)\n        - HH: Hour (00-23, 24-hour format)\n        - MM: Minute (00-59)\n        - SS: Second (00-59)\n        Example: "2024:03:15:14:30:00" = March 15, 2024 at 2:30 PM\n\nReturns:\n    bool: Alarm status:\n    - True: Alarm successfully scheduled\n    - False: Invalid time format, past time, duplicate alarm, \n             or invalid date componen